---
alwaysApply: false
description: Use baby steps for complex tasks
---
Implementing a new entity is a complex task! The process is prone to error if not done correctly and in a rushed way. 
To ensure success, we will always use a "baby steps" approach (i.e. one step at a time).
That means you will perform a step then wait for the user to give feedback. 
If the user wants changes, you will implement them. 
If not, the user will give you the green light to move to the next step.
you will make an effort to actually stick to this (baby step) approach until the end. It will not get ahead of itself and start implementing multiple steps at a time halfway though. 
Remember: implement step --> get feedback --> apply feedback (if necessary) --> get green light --> implement next step.